From 232849c87d808235478f55c3e0748d07cfb884c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cruz <cruz@tbu.net>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 09:34:10 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 147/206] comment: A5's conclusion does not survive counting
 their emitted instructions

The note above the early return said resolution is the only path Shorebird's IL
pass uses, because a mapping-only file yields 0 rewrite sites for their binary
and a voters-only file yields the expected ones. Running their gen_snapshot and
counting what it emitted says otherwise:

  theirs, voters.bin supplied : 92 dispatch sites
  theirs, no input at all     : 92
  ours,   voters.bin supplied :  3
  ours,   no input at all      :  0

Counted as `ldr x30, [x26, xN]`, with 92 of 92 preceded by an untagging asr and
followed by `blr x30`, and every one of them inside a listed function body
rather than an inherited stub. The voters file drives resolution, not emission.

A5 was reading rewrite-site counters; this reads the instructions that came
out. Both can be right about what they measured, and only one of them answers
whether we diverge.

No behaviour change here. What selects their 92 sites is still unknown and
rewriting unconditionally would overshoot -- 84 of 1380 optimized functions
carry one. Tracked as F34.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc b/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc
index 4e96b75b40f..131d9f62fa8 100644
--- a/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc
+++ b/runtime/vm/compiler/aot/aot_call_specializer.cc
@@ -1220,10 +1220,26 @@ void AotCallSpecializer::ReplaceInstanceCallsWithDispatchTableCalls() {
 // mapping first also leaves the production configuration -- voters and mapping
 // supplied together -- with exactly the behaviour it had before this note.
 void AotCallSpecializer::ReplaceStaticCallsWithIndirectStaticCalls() {
-  // Resolution is the only path Shorebird's IL pass uses (A5): a file with
-  // only a DDSlotMapping section gives 0 rewrite sites for their binary, while
-  // a voters-only file gives the expected sites. The kernel_offset path was
-  // removed once this was confirmed by experiment.
+  // A5 said resolution is the only path Shorebird's IL pass uses, on the
+  // grounds that a mapping-only file gives 0 rewrite sites for their binary
+  // while a voters-only file gives the expected ones. Measured against their
+  // emitted instructions on 2026-09-08, that conclusion does not hold:
+  //
+  //   their gen_snapshot, voters.bin supplied : 92 dispatch sites
+  //   their gen_snapshot, no input at all     : 92 dispatch sites
+  //   ours,               voters.bin supplied :  3
+  //   ours,               no input at all     :  0
+  //
+  // Counted as `ldr x30, [x26, xN]` -- 92 of 92 preceded by `asr xN,xN,#1` and
+  // followed by `blr x30`, and all 92 inside listed function bodies rather
+  // than inherited stubs. So the voters file drives resolution, not emission,
+  // and the early return below is a divergence from them rather than a gate
+  // they also have. A5 measured rewrite-site counters; this measures the
+  // instructions that actually came out.
+  //
+  // Left in place deliberately: what selects their 92 sites is not known yet,
+  // and rewriting unconditionally would overshoot badly -- only 84 of 1380
+  // optimized functions carry one. Tracked as F34.
   const DDSlotResolution* resolution = ShorebirdLinker::shared()->resolution();
   if (resolution == nullptr) return;
 
